343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 212 0 R
/T (Accountants acting as formation agents perform the critical function of establishing legal persons or arrangements, including the preparation and filing of incorporation documents with the Registrar of Companies. This role carries significant money laundering and terrorist financing \(ML/TF\) risks, as these services are often exploited to achieve anonymity through shell companies, nominees, or jurisdictions with weak transparency. Without robust customer due diligence and verification of beneficial ownership, accountants risk unknowingly facilitating the creation of  structures designed to mask criminal activity.)
/E (Accountants acting as formation agents perform the critical function of establishing legal persons or arrangements, including the preparation and filing of incorporation documents with the Registrar of Companies. This role carries significant money laundering and terrorist financing \(ML/TF\) risks, as these services are often exploited to achieve anonymity through shell companies, nominees, or jurisdictions with weak transparency. Without robust customer due diligence and verification of beneficial ownership, accountants risk unknowingly facilitating the creation of  structures designed to mask criminal activity.)
