/P 213 0 R
/T (This activity applies to accountants in public practice if they provide this service to their clients who are legal persons or if they find persons and prepare or file the necessary documentation for another person to perform this service for their clients. Acting as a nominee shareholder, or arranging such services, directly obscures beneficial ownership by holding shares on behalf of another person. This practice poses a high ML/TF risk because it enables individuals to control companies without being publicly identified. Nominee arrangements particularly when combined with offshore entities or layered ownership structures, can significantly impede transparency and are commonly associated with sophisticated money laundering schemes.)
/E (This activity applies to accountants in public practice if they provide this service to their clients who are legal persons or if they find persons and prepare or file the necessary documentation for another person to perform this service for their clients. Acting as a nominee shareholder, or arranging such services, directly obscures beneficial ownership by holding shares on behalf of another person. This practice poses a high ML/TF risk because it enables individuals to control companies without being publicly identified. Nominee arrangements particularly when combined with offshore entities or layered ownership structures, can significantly impede transparency and are commonly associated with sophisticated money laundering schemes.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8 9]
