/T (Accountants in Kenya must strictly adhere to the preventative obligations under POCAMLA, POTA, and their supporting regulations. Under Section 44 of POCAMLA and Regulation 38 of the POCAML-Regulations \(2023\), Accountants are required to file Suspicious Transaction Reports \(STRs\) or Suspicious Activity Reports \(SAR\) with FRC. Consequently, this Guidance is designed to assist practitioners, particularly those performing high-risk activities, in identifying and reporting illicit financial patterns to ensure full regulatory compliance and protect the integrity of the profession.)
/E (Accountants in Kenya must strictly adhere to the preventative obligations under POCAMLA, POTA, and their supporting regulations. Under Section 44 of POCAMLA and Regulation 38 of the POCAML-Regulations \(2023\), Accountants are required to file Suspicious Transaction Reports \(STRs\) or Suspicious Activity Reports \(SAR\) with FRC. Consequently, this Guidance is designed to assist practitioners, particularly those performing high-risk activities, in identifying and reporting illicit financial patterns to ensure full regulatory compliance and protect the integrity of the profession.)
