/P 220 0 R
/E (Audit and Accounting firms should understand the type of clients that they serve. To identify potential risks, these firms must evaluate their client base against the following risk factors and red-flag indicators. The presence of one or more indicators may signal a heightened risk of money laundering, terrorist financing, or proliferation financing. Because these indicators are not exhaustive and may apply to various scenarios on a case-by-case basis, accountants must maintain an "inquiring mind" and exercise professional skepticism throughout both the initial client due diligence and the ongoing monitoring of the engagement.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [18]
>>
