1105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 243 0 R
/T (Over time, the accounting firm experienced persistent delays and resistance when requesting ownership information, trust deeds, and supporting documentation. Complete accounting records were only submitted after repeated follow-ups and covered three consecutive years at once, limiting effective ongoing monitoring. Upon reviewing the records, JIM Advisory LLP identified several red flags. The Group frequently invested in Kenyan and regional start-ups, only to dispose of these investments within short periods, almost always at a profit, without clear commercial explanations. Gift Group companies operated multiple bank accounts in Kenya and abroad, with funds being transferred almost immediately upon receipt, often between related entities. Management consultancy invoices were predominantly issued to foreign related companies in a high-risk jurisdiction, and the firm later discovered that Mr. Yang, the suspected beneficial owner, sat on the executive committee of some of the invoiced entities. Taken together, the opaque ownership structure, high-risk jurisdictions, rapid movement of funds, related-party invoicing, and possible politically exposed person \(PEP\) involvement raised reasonable suspicion.)
/E (Over time, the accounting firm experienced persistent delays and resistance when requesting ownership information, trust deeds, and supporting documentation. Complete accounting records were only submitted after repeated follow-ups and covered three consecutive years at once, limiting effective ongoing monitoring. Upon reviewing the records, JIM Advisory LLP identified several red flags. The Group frequently invested in Kenyan and regional start-ups, only to dispose of these investments within short periods, almost always at a profit, without clear commercial explanations. Gift Group companies operated multiple bank accounts in Kenya and abroad, with funds being transferred almost immediately upon receipt, often between related entities. Management consultancy invoices were predominantly issued to foreign related companies in a high-risk jurisdiction, and the firm later discovered that Mr. Yang, the suspected beneficial owner, sat on the executive committee of some of the invoiced entities. Taken together, the opaque ownership structure, high-risk jurisdictions, rapid movement of funds, related-party invoicing, and possible politically exposed person \(PEP\) involvement raised reasonable suspicion.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
