/T (When accountants act as, or arrange others to act as, company directors, secretaries, or partners, they may provide administrative or governance support. These arrangements can be misused to create a buffer between the true controller and the entity, enabling criminals to exercise control while remaining hidden. This lack of transparency can undermine corporate governance and allow legal persons to be used as vehicles for money laundering or terrorist financing without effective oversight.)
/E (When accountants act as, or arrange others to act as, company directors, secretaries, or partners, they may provide administrative or governance support. These arrangements can be misused to create a buffer between the true controller and the entity, enabling criminals to exercise control while remaining hidden. This lack of transparency can undermine corporate governance and allow legal persons to be used as vehicles for money laundering or terrorist financing without effective oversight.)
